<% content_for :title, "Pricing — Printwright" %>
<div class="container" style="max-width: 720px">
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <p class="t-small muted">The real economics, not a rate card — there is no paid tier here to
    upsell.</p>

  <h2>Designers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You set your own per-print price on every license offer.</li>
    <li>You keep <strong>90%</strong> of every sale; the platform fee is <strong>10%</strong>
      (recorded per-sale in an immutable ledger, visible on your statement).</li>
    <li>Each buyer payment settles to Printwright's treasury. After delivery, your 90% share is
      queued to your verified payout destination. If that payout cannot complete, the share
      remains owed in treasury with transaction proof on your statement.</li>
    <li>No listing fees, no subscription.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Buyers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pay the offer price, settled on-chain in HBAR or USDC on Hedera
      <%= Hedera::Network.name %>. No card processing, no account required for the agent
      door.</li>
    <li>Network fees — a fraction of a cent per purchase — are paid by the facilitator, not
      added to the offer price.</li>
    <li>The opaque licence commitment submitted to Hedera Consensus Service costs about $0.0008
      plus payload-byte extras at the current published fee schedule; that cost is absorbed by
      the platform, not billed separately.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Settlement</h2>
  <p>Buyer settlement is separate from buyer delivery and designer payout. A pending or held
    designer payout does not delay or revoke the buyer's delivered licence. Every real payment is
    a Hedera <%= Hedera::Network.name %> transaction; after delivery, a separate asynchronous
    transaction anchors the licence's opaque commitment. See the <%= link_to "API docs", docs_path %>
    for the exact negotiation.</p>
</div>
